and you just got hit, and you're down to one hit point, and you're kind of frantically searching through your inventory, oh my god, do I read this scroll?

275
00:24:49,184 --> 00:24:50,525
I don't even have it identified.

276
00:24:50,545 --> 00:24:54,186
I don't know what it's going to do here, but I got like one chance to do something.

277
00:24:54,306 --> 00:24:55,686
Should I drink a poke?

278
00:24:55,706 --> 00:24:56,526
Do I run away?

279
00:24:56,626 --> 00:24:58,607
Oh my god, I'm at a dead end.

280
00:24:58,867 --> 00:25:00,167
I mean, your palms are swaying.

281
00:25:00,407 --> 00:25:02,028
I've been working on this character for two weeks.

282
00:25:02,408 --> 00:25:03,528
My god, what am I going to do?

283
00:25:03,608 --> 00:25:05,689
And you've got to get up and walk away from the computer.

284
00:25:06,689 --> 00:25:07,109
I don't know.

285
00:25:07,129 --> 00:25:08,710
And then, of course, you're dead.

286
00:25:11,379 --> 00:25:12,660
the tears would flow for a second.

287
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:15,861
All right, let's play again.

288
00:25:16,621 --> 00:25:18,402
And so I really loved that tension.

289
00:25:18,422 --> 00:25:23,224
I really loved the sweaty palms of I've been working on this thing and I'm about to lose two weeks of work.

290
00:25:23,964 --> 00:25:25,505
So I didn't want to lose that at all.

291
00:25:25,865 --> 00:25:31,647
And they said, yeah, but, you know, real time will be better.

292
00:25:34,388 --> 00:25:35,009
Okay.

293
00:25:35,109 --> 00:25:36,029
Well, if you say so.

294
00:25:36,089 --> 00:25:37,350
So they started

295
00:25:38,892 --> 00:25:44,735
going around talking to other people in the studio, and other people in the studio, and yeah, we should make this thing real time.

296
00:25:46,195 --> 00:25:56,720
And so I kind of held out, there were about two or three of us that held out to the bitter end, and finally one day we decided to have a talk and bring it to a vote.

297
00:25:57,640 --> 00:26:02,863
So we all met in the kitchen, and we voted, and I voted no, and everybody else voted yes.

298
00:26:05,785 --> 00:26:10,828
And so I said, all right, well, OK, I guess we can do this.

299
00:26:10,888 --> 00:26:18,653
But I called up Blizzard South, and I said, well, as you guys will see in a few minutes, we were terrible businessmen.

300
00:26:18,673 --> 00:26:22,175
But this is a huge delay in the project.

301
00:26:23,996 --> 00:26:25,157
It's going to take us a long time.

302
00:26:25,177 --> 00:26:27,098
We have to redo all sorts of things.

303
00:26:27,158 --> 00:26:28,739
It's going to take me forever to write this.

304
00:26:31,152 --> 00:26:37,936
I, you know, okay, alright, yeah, but we need another milestone payment out of this, but yeah, okay, we'll go ahead and do it.

305
00:26:37,976 --> 00:26:44,099
So they agreed to this, yes, and so, okay, I'll do this.

306
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:51,563
So I sat down on a Friday afternoon and in a few hours I had it running.

307
00:26:57,626 --> 00:26:57,746
And

308
00:26:59,479 --> 00:27:06,386
And so I can remember, yes, this is what went right.

309
00:27:09,049 --> 00:27:11,691
I can remember the moment that this happened.

