00:27:14,394 --> 00:27:17,217
This is like one of the most vivid moments of my career.

312
00:27:19,575 --> 00:27:40,628
I was sitting there and I finally got, you know, all the kind of, because the turn base was basically already, everything took different amounts of turns, I just like put in some stuff for moving around, took time, was it basically a certain amount of turns and then just made the turns happen 20 times a second or whatever it was and then it all just kind of worked magically.

313
00:27:42,109 --> 00:27:48,533
And so I remember taking the mouse and I clicked on the mouse

314
00:27:50,428 --> 00:27:58,297
and the warrior walked over and smacked the skeleton down and I was like, oh my god!

315
00:27:58,317 --> 00:28:01,902
That was awesome!

316
00:28:13,140 --> 00:28:31,274
and the sun shone through the window, and gods passed by, and the angels sung, and sure enough, that was when the ARPG was kind of born at that moment, and I was lucky enough to be there.

317
00:28:31,334 --> 00:28:32,916
It was an amazing, amazing moment.

318
00:28:32,976 --> 00:28:33,736
I'll never forget it.

319
00:28:35,618 --> 00:28:51,885
And so that was really kind of the birth and really a big turning point in the project and this was pretty early on this was still This is still probably about maybe five months in or six months in that that we had done this What we're wrong budget

